<title>FRANCE: GAN workers protest planned job cuts.</title>
<headline>GAN workers protest planned job cuts.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Several hundred employees of French state insurer Groupe GAN marched through the streets of Paris on Thursday in protest against plans to restructure the firm before privatising it later this year.</p>
<p>Police said 850 GAN workers marched from GAN headquarters to the National Assembly, where they presented a petition demanding a withdrawal of management's social plan to a group of opposition Socialist and Communist deputies.</p>
<p>The plan proposes eliminating 591 jobs by June 1998, union officials said. GAN's workforce currently totals 8,500.</p>
<p>Groupe des Assurances Nationale (GAN) has run up huge losses in recent years on property loans and insurance underwriting.</p>
<p>The French state plans a 20 billion franc rescue of the state-controlled insurer before selling it later this year.</p>
</text>
